# UrbanCool-AI — Chennai UHI Mitigation Planner

AI-based Urban Heat Island mitigation planner for Chennai, India. Uses Landsat 8 satellite data via Google Earth Engine to detect heat islands, identify tree-planting priorities, simulate cooling impacts, and rank optimal plantation zones.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The existing [.env](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/.env) has `GEE_PRIVATE_KEY` but the spec requires `GEE_KEY_PATH`. I will add `GEE_KEY_PATH` as an alias pointing to the same [service-account.json](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/service-account.json) file, and the code will look for `GEE_KEY_PATH` first, falling back to `GEE_PRIVATE_KEY`.

> [!WARNING]
> GEE export tasks (`Export.image.toDrive`) are asynchronous and can take minutes to hours. For the V1 prototype, all GEE processing will compute results server-side via `getInfo()` and download locally using `geemap` or `ee.Image.getDownloadURL()` for reasonable-sized areas. This avoids waiting for GEE Drive exports.

## Proposed Changes

### Directory Structure

Create the required empty directories: `src/`, `app/`, `data/raw/`, `outputs/`, `models/`.

---

### Authentication Module

#### [MODIFY] [.env](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/.env)
- Add `GEE_KEY_PATH=service-account.json` variable

#### [NEW] [auth.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/auth.py)
- Load [.env](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/.env), initialize GEE with service account credentials
- Return authenticated `ee` object via `initialize_gee()` function

#### [NEW] [utils.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/utils.py)
- Chennai bounding box & config constants
- Helper functions: `get_chennai_boundary()`, `save_geotiff()`, `ensure_dirs()`

---

### Satellite Data Extraction

#### [NEW] [gee_extraction.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/gee_extraction.py)
- Extract Chennai boundary (bounding box or FAO GAUL)
- Filter Landsat 8 C02 L2 by date (2025-04-01 to 2025-07-31) and bounds
- Apply cloud masking using QA_PIXEL
- Extract ST_B10, convert to Celsius (scale factor 0.00341802 + offset 149.0 - 273.15)
- Compute mean LST composite
- Export `outputs/lst.tif`

---

### NDVI Module

#### [NEW] [ndvi.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/ndvi.py)
- Compute NDVI = (SR_B5 - SR_B4) / (SR_B5 + SR_B4)
- Classify: Dense (>0.6), Moderate (0.3–0.6), Sparse (0.1–0.3), Built-up (<0.1)
- Export `outputs/ndvi.tif`

---

### Heat Classification

#### [NEW] [heat_classification.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/heat_classification.py)
- Compute mean LST, then classify pixels relative to mean:
  - Cool (< mean-2°C), Moderate (mean-2 to mean), Warm (mean to mean+2), Hot (mean+2 to mean+4), Extreme (> mean+4)
- Export `outputs/heat_classification.tif`

---

### Cooling Index

#### [NEW] [cooling_index.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/cooling_index.py)
- Compute: `CI = 0.5*TreeCanopy + 0.25*NDVI + 0.15*Albedo + 0.10*DistToWater`
- Tree canopy proxy from NDVI thresholds; Albedo from visible bands; Distance to water from JRC water dataset
- Normalize 0–1
- Export `outputs/cooling_index.tif`

---

### Tree Need Analysis

#### [NEW] [tree_need_analysis.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/tree_need_analysis.py)
- Combine heat class + NDVI + impervious surface proxy
- Classify: 0=Low, 1=Moderate, 2=High need
- High need = (Hot/Extreme heat AND NDVI<0.3 AND high impervious)
- Export `outputs/tree_need_map.tif`

---

### Machine Learning

#### [NEW] [ml_model.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/ml_model.py)
- Sample pixel features: LST, NDVI, distance to coast, distance to road, impervious proxy
- Target: simulated ΔT from cooling index
- Train `RandomForestRegressor`
- Evaluate: R², RMSE, feature importance
- Save model to `models/rf_model.pkl`
- Export metrics to `outputs/model_metrics.json`

---

### Scenario Simulation

#### [NEW] [scenario_simulation.py](file:///c:/Users/welcome/OneDrive/Desktop/UrbanCool-AI/src/scenario_simulation.py)
- Simulate +10% canopy increase
- Recalculate new mean LST, % extreme heat reduction, average cooling
- Export `outputs/scenario_results.json`

---

### Plantation Ranking (integrated into ml_model.py)

- Filter Hot/Extreme heat zones with NDVI<0.3
- Predict ΔT with trained model
- Select top 200 zones
- Export `outputs/top_plantation_spots.csv` and `outputs/top_plantation_spots.geojson`

---

